{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וענתה", :translit "v'antah", :gloss "and her [conjugal] due"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling (missing vav) signals that the essence of the conjugal right falls on Shabbat."}], :frame {:text "The weekly conjugal obligation (onah) is fundamentally a Shabbat obligation. Ketubot 62b records the rabbinic schedule of conjugal duties, and the Talmud establishes Shabbat as the designated time for those whose obligation is once weekly. By reading וענתה in its defective spelling, Ba'al HaTurim ties the orthographic deficiency to this halakhic prioritization of Shabbat over weekdays.", :sources ["Ketubot 62b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling (missing vav) signals that the essence of the conjugal right falls on Shabbat.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:17:52.584443209Z", :model "glm-5.2"}